-- title:
--   Compact open maximal order in a twisted commutant
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra of degree $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = 2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion of $K$, let $c \in K_v^{\times}$, and let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Assume $\delta$ is a norm of the scalar matrix with diagonal entry $c$ in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.IsNormOf`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L217), i.e. there is $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ with the image of that scalar matrix under `toTensorGL` equal to $y^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{normString}(\delta) \cdot y$, and assume that for no $z \in (L \otimes_K K_v)^{\times}$ is $\delta$ $\sigma$-conjugate to the scalar matrix with entry $z$, that is, the scalar matrix is never of the form $x^{-1} \delta\, \sigma(x)$ with $\sigma$ acting on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ entrywise through $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}_{K_v}$. Let $D = \{x \in M_2(L \otimes_K K_v) \mid x \delta = \delta \cdot (\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})(x)\}$ be the twisted commutant, and let $O \subseteq M_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ be the set of $x \in D$ such that either $x = 0$ or $\det x = 1 \otimes s$ for some $s \in K_v^{\times}$ with $|s|_v \le 1$. The conclusion is threefold: $O$ is compact; $O = V \cap D$ for some open $V \subseteq M_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$; and an invertible matrix $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ lies in $O$ exactly when $x \in D$ and, for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$, $\det x = 1 \otimes s$ with $s \in K_v^{\times}$ of valuation $\mathrm{exp}(-n)$.
--
--   At a place $v$ of the second kind, where $\delta$ has scalar norm string but is not $\sigma$-conjugate to a scalar, the twisted commutant is a quaternion division algebra over $K_v$ with reduced norm the determinant, and $O$ is its maximal order; the statement records that this order is compact, relatively open in the commutant, and has unit group the union of the non-negative determinant shells. It supplies the topological input for the choice of local level at such a place and for the comparison of integrals over the twisted centraliser.
